sentences.text:
This Court has considered the following facts while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant :-
(i) the applicant is in jail since 14.12.2023;
(ii) the investigation is over and the charge-sheet is filed;
(iii) though the scam is a big scam, however, it was submitted by learned advocate Mr. Koshti that in the applicant's account, only Rs.19 Lacs were deposited out of which the applicant is beneficiary of Rs.1.5 Lacs and the aforesaid facts could not be disputed by learned APP from the charge-sheet papers;

Hence, present application is allowed and the applicant is ordered to be released on regular bail in connection with the FIR being C.R.No.11202058230003 of 2023 registered with Cyber Crime Police Station, District Jamnagar on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he shall;
[a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty; [b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
[d] not leave the territorial limits of Gujarat State without prior permission of the Sessions Judge concerned;
[e] furnish latest address of residence to the Investigating Officer and also to the Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior permission of the trial Court;
Kumar S/O Jitendrabhai Prajapati vs State Of Gujarat on 7 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/85219071/
2 [f] mark his presence before the concerned police station in the first week of every month till the trial is over;
NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/25645/2024 ORDER DATED: 07/02/2025 undefined 7.

